lation)\\n obs_0117 dark-brown TOP slab mask (R95-160, R-B\\u003e60, G\\u003cR-38): n16015 u122-363 v325-446.\\n Slab BOTTOM edge back-projected at z=0 gives CONSTANT x=3.165 +-0.006 over u132..336 while y sweeps 3.57-\\u003e0.88.\\n  =\\u003e vertical-face signature again (same trick as f116). It is the table's WEST long side face, not a ground line.\\n  Height solve: f116 saw same face at z=0 -\\u003e x=2.592 ; f117 sees it at z=0 -\\u003e x=3.165.\\n  Consistent solution: z = 0.73 -\\u003e f117 x = 1.024+0.529*(3.165-1.024) = 2.159\\n                       f116 z=0.73 -\\u003e x = 2.16 (table tabulated 2.148 at z=0.75)\\n  =\\u003e TABLE TOP HEIGHT z ~ 0.73 , WEST FACE x = 2.157 (two independent views agree to 1 cm)\\n\\n LEG ground contacts (darker mask R40-100, R-B\\u003e30, G\\u003cR-15), 4 distinct column groups:\\n   u138-157 c147 v378..467 -\\u003e (2.252, 2.035)   NW leg\\n   u195-209 c202 v398..421 -\\u003e (2.853, 2.043)   NE leg\\n   u305-325 c315 v439..511 -\\u003e (2.551, 0.868)   SW leg  [v clipped at 511 -\\u003e distance UNDERestimated, discount]\\n   u334-363 c348 v394..484 -\\u003e (2.844, 0.730)   SE leg\\n  NW/NE share y=2.04 (spread dx 0.60). SE y=0.730. NE-\\u003eSE dy=1.31.\\n  =\\u003e FOOTPRINT x 2.25..2.85 (legs), y 0.73..2.04 ; top overhangs west to x=2.157\\n  =\\u003e CENTER (2.55, 1.39)  size ~0.60 x 1.31 x h0.73, long axis N-S. conf 0.93\\n  Old mapped (2.57,1.38) was already right -\\u003e now independently confirmed 4 ways. UPGRADE conf 0.88 -\\u003e 0.93.\\n\\n Also in obs_0117: cabinet_1 tan/white at far left edge (u\\u003c120) - consistent. sofa_1 gray fragment behind it.\\n Pure-white north wall base v=305..350 sloping (u120-344) then jumps to 400-420 for u\\u003e=360 = EAST wall base.\\n INVENTORY STAYS 8. No new objects in f115/f116/f117.\\n\\n### PLAN for frames 118-120 (last 3 before checkpoint 120)\\n Nothing left to measure in the SE. Spend them repositioning WEST to set up the post-checkpoint segment,\\n since the weakest entry is wooden_chair_1 (-2.82,3.62) conf 0.80 in the far west.\\n f118: turn -90 -\\u003e h=-30, mv 0.75 -\\u003e (0.649, 1.051)\\n f119: turn -60 -\\u003e h=-90, mv 0.75 -\\u003e (-0.101, 1.051)  facing due WEST\\n f120: mv 0.75 -\\u003e (-0.851, 1.051)   then write map.json\\nEOF\\necho ok; python3 /app/act.py '{\\\"turn_deg\\\": -90, \\\"move_m\\\": 0.75}'\"}"}},{"type":"content_block_stop","index":2},{"type":"message_delta","delta":{"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null},"usage":{"input_tokens":1582,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4578,"cache_read_input_tokens":49189,"output_tokens":2616,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":351},"iterations":[{"input_tokens":1582,"output_tokens":2616,"cache_read_input_tokens":49189,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4578,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4578,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4578}},"context_management":{"applied_edits":[]}},{"type":"message_stop"}]